lour first—mise en place makes this dessert twice as fast."},{"stepNumber":2,"phaseLabel":"Build Flavor","title":"Simmer & Dissolve Smoothly","instructionTemplate":"Meanwhile, make the rice pudding by putting the rice with sugar, milk and vanilla extract in a saucepan. Add the cardamom, star anise and cinnamon. Bring to a boil and cook, stirring constantly. Take out the spices. In a small bowl, mix baking soda with lemon juice/apple vinegar. Stir well until baking soda is dissolved, then mix into the rice pudding. Incorporate {m53391_5}, {m53391_6}, and {m53391_7} smoothly until evenly distributed.","durationMin":5,"timerSeconds":300,"activeMeasureSummary":"Vegetable Millk, Yeast"},{"stepNumber":3,"phaseLabel":"Combine & Fold","title":"Combine Wet & Dry Smoothly","instructionTemplate":"Fold {m53391_8}, {m53391_9}, {m53391_10}, {m53391_11}, {m53391_12}, {m53391_13}, and {m53391_14} into the base in two additions using gentle strokes until glossy and uniform with zero dry pockets. Avoid overmixing so the final texture stays light and tender.","durationMin":3,"timerSeconds":180,"activeMeasureSummary":"Glossy Batter • Zero Lumps"},{"stepNumber":4,"phaseLabel":"Shape & Layer","title":"Shape & Press Dough Evenly","instructionTemplate":"Roll out the dough on a floured work surface (it is very sticky, but don’t stress it will be fine) and line the bottom and edges of a greased mold with it. Spread the rice pudding over the bottom and bake for about 25 to 30 minutes.","durationMin":30,"timerSeconds":1800,"activeMeasureSummary":"Sugar, Dessert Rice","criticalTip":"Let set for 5–10 minutes before slicing or plating so the textures hold crisp and photogenic!","creatorSecret":"Chill the filled crust 10 minutes before baking—cold butter hits the hot oven and puffs into extra-flaky layers."}],"ugcQuotes":[{"id":"muq-53391","handle":"@baker_traditio","image":"./ai-images/traditional-dutch-rice-tart-rijstevlaai.jpg","quote":"Followed the scaled metric steps—came out flawless in 45 mins!","rating":5}]}}]
